<!-- ══════════════════ SECTION 3 ══════════════════ -->
<h1>3. Database Architecture &amp; Connectivity</h1>

<h2>3.1 Connection Strategy &amp; Resilience</h2>
<p>
  The database is hosted on Supabase's managed PostgreSQL infrastructure located in the <span class="highlight">aws-0-ap-southeast-1</span> region. Connection management is governed through the <strong>PgBouncer Transaction Pooler</strong> on port <span class="highlight">6543</span>.
</p>

<div class="card-box">
  <div class="card-box-title">Critical Architectural Solution: URL Dotted Username Handling</div>
  <p>
    Supabase transaction pooler URLs format the username as <span class="highlight">postgres.[project-ref]</span>. Default URL parsers erroneously interpret the dot as a hostname separator, resulting in runtime <span class="highlight">ENOTFOUND tenant/user</span> errors. In <span class="highlight">src/lib/db.ts</span>, discrete URL parameters are parsed programmatically and supplied directly into the connection pool:
  </p>
  <div class="code-block">const sql = postgres({
  host: urlObj.hostname,
  port: urlObj.port ? Number(urlObj.port) : 6543,
  username: decodeURIComponent(urlObj.username),
  password: decodeURIComponent(urlObj.password),
  database: urlObj.pathname.replace(/^\//, "") || "postgres",
  max: 10,
  idle_timeout: 20,
  connect_timeout: 15,
  ssl: "require",
});</div>
</div>

<h2>3.2 Atomic Financial Transactions</h2>
<p>
  For complex operations in the Accounts-Web general ledger, multi-split journal entries require absolute ACID compliance. AccBots employs atomic transaction boundaries (<span class="highlight">sql.begin(async (tx) =&gt; { ... })</span>) to ensure that if a credit or debit entry fails, all corresponding insertions are rolled back immediately, preserving mathematical integrity.
</p>

<h2>3.3 Complete Schema &amp; Table Reference</h2>
<p>
  The database is organized into 15 normalized tables and 1 dynamic view spanning four operational modules:
</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Table Name</th>
      <th>Primary Purpose</th>
      <th>Key Columns &amp; Data Types</th>
      <th>Constraints &amp; Foreign Keys</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>users</strong></td>
      <td>Central user account store</td>
      <td>id (UUID), full_name (TEXT), email (TEXT), password_hash (TEXT), role (TEXT), is_active (BOOL)</td>
      <td>PK: id, UNIQUE: email, CHECK: role in ('super_admin', 'admin', 'user')</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>refresh_tokens</strong></td>
      <td>Session persistence &amp; revocation</td>
      <td>id (UUID), user_id (UUID), token_hash (TEXT), expires_at (TIMESTAMPTZ), revoked_at (TIMESTAMPTZ)</td>
      <td>FK: user_id -&gt; users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE, UNIQUE: token_hash</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>password_reset_tokens</strong></td>
      <td>Cryptographic password recovery</td>
      <td>id (UUID), user_id (UUID), token_hash (TEXT), expires_at (TIMESTAMPTZ), used_at (TIMESTAMPTZ)</td>
      <td>FK: user_id -&gt; users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE, UNIQUE: token_hash</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>contact_messages</strong></td>
      <td>Lead capture from public forms</td>
      <td>id (UUID), name (TEXT), email (TEXT), phone (TEXT), subject (TEXT), message (TEXT), is_read (BOOL)</td>
      <td>PK: id, INDEX: created_at DESC, is_read</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>services</strong></td>
      <td>Advisory service packages</td>
      <td>id (UUID), title (TEXT), slug (TEXT), icon (TEXT), short_description (TEXT), benefits (TEXT[]), process_steps (JSONB), faqs (JSONB)</td>
      <td>PK: id, UNIQUE: slug, INDEX: is_active, sort_order</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>website_settings</strong></td>
      <td>Dynamic site configuration</td>
      <td>id (UUID), key (TEXT), value (TEXT), category (TEXT), updated_at (TIMESTAMPTZ)</td>
      <td>PK: id, UNIQUE: key, CHECK: category in ('general', 'contact', 'seo', 'social')</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>testimonials</strong></td>
      <td>Client ratings &amp; reviews</td>
      <td>id (UUID), name (TEXT), company (TEXT), role (TEXT), content (TEXT), avatar_url (TEXT), rating (INT)</td>
      <td>PK: id, CHECK: rating &gt;= 1 and rating &lt;= 5</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>team_members</strong></td>
      <td>Executive leadership bios</td>
      <td>id (UUID), name (TEXT), role (TEXT), bio (TEXT), avatar_url (TEXT), linkedin_url (TEXT)</td>
      <td>PK: id, INDEX: sort_order</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>blog_posts</strong></td>
      <td>CMS knowledge base articles</td>
      <td>id (UUID), title (TEXT), slug (TEXT), excerpt (TEXT), content (TEXT), cover_image (TEXT), is_published (BOOL)</td>
      <td>PK: id, UNIQUE: slug, FK: author_id -&gt; users(id)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>activity_logs</strong></td>
      <td>Security and audit tracking</td>
      <td>id (UUID), user_id (UUID), action (TEXT), entity_type (TEXT), entity_id (TEXT), metadata (JSONB), ip_address (TEXT)</td>
      <td>PK: id, FK: user_id -&gt; users(id) ON DELETE SET NULL</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>expense_categories</strong></td>
      <td>Budget classification</td>
      <td>id (UUID), name (TEXT), description (TEXT), budget_limit (NUMERIC(12,2)), is_active (BOOL)</td>
      <td>PK: id, UNIQUE: name</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>expenses</strong></td>
      <td>Corporate expense filings</td>
      <td>id (UUID), user_id (UUID), category_id (UUID), amount (NUMERIC(12,2)), currency (TEXT), receipt_url (TEXT), status (TEXT)</td>
      <td>PK: id, FK: user_id -&gt; users, FK: category_id -&gt; expense_categories, CHECK: status in ('pending','approved','rejected')</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>accounts</strong></td>
      <td>General Ledger Chart of Accounts</td>
      <td>id (UUID), code (TEXT), name (TEXT), type (TEXT), currency (TEXT), is_active (BOOL)</td>
      <td>PK: id, UNIQUE: code, CHECK: type in ('asset','liability','equity','revenue','expense')</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>transactions</strong></td>
      <td>Journal voucher headers</td>
      <td>id (UUID), reference_number (TEXT), description (TEXT), transaction_date (DATE), created_by (UUID)</td>
      <td>PK: id, UNIQUE: reference_number, FK: created_by -&gt; users(id)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>journal_entries</strong></td>
      <td>Double-entry debit/credit splits</td>
      <td>id (UUID), transaction_id (UUID), account_id (UUID), debit (NUMERIC(12,2)), credit (NUMERIC(12,2)), description (TEXT)</td>
      <td>PK: id, FK: transaction_id -&gt; transactions CASCADE, FK: account_id -&gt; accounts RESTRICT, CHECK: balanced splits</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>trial_balance (View)</strong></td>
      <td>Dynamic accounting trial balance</td>
      <td>account_id (UUID), code (TEXT), name (TEXT), type (TEXT), total_debit (NUMERIC), total_credit (NUMERIC), net_balance (NUMERIC)</td>
      <td>Calculated in real-time via SQL aggregation over journal_entries joined with accounts.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- ══════════════════ SECTION 4 ══════════════════ -->
<h1>4. Security Architecture &amp; Perimeter Defense</h1>
<p>
  AccBots implements a multi-layered defense model across network, session, application, and database boundaries:
</p>

<h2>4.1 HTTP Security Headers</h2>
<p>
  Configured in <span class="highlight">next.config.ts</span>, all outgoing responses enforce strict security headers to prevent prevalent web vulnerabilities:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff</strong> — Prevents MIME-type sniffing by browsers.</li>
  <li><strong>X-Frame-Options: DENY</strong> — Completely protects the application against clickjacking by disallowing iframe embedding.</li>
  <li><strong>X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block</strong> — Activates legacy browser anti-XSS filtering.</li>
  <li><strong>Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin</strong> — Conceals sensitive URL parameters on cross-origin navigation.</li>
  <li><strong>Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()</strong> — Disables hardware access from the browser.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4.2 Custom Stateless JWT &amp; Cookie Security</h2>
<p>
  Authentication is handled without third-party vendor lock-in:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Short-Lived Access Tokens (15 Minutes):</strong> Signed using <span class="highlight">jose</span> with the HS256 algorithm and a minimum 64-character secret key.</li>
  <li><strong>Hashed Long-Lived Refresh Tokens (7–30 Days):</strong> To allow immediate revocation, refresh tokens are hashed using SHA-256 before insertion into <span class="highlight">refresh_tokens</span>. Raw token values are never stored in the database.</li>
  <li><strong>HttpOnly &amp; SameSite Cookies:</strong> Tokens are stored in <span class="highlight">HttpOnly</span>, <span class="highlight">Secure</span> (in production), and <span class="highlight">SameSite=Lax</span> cookies (<span class="highlight">accbot_access_token</span> and <span class="highlight">accbot_refresh_token</span>), eliminating JavaScript token theft via XSS.</li>
  <li><strong>Silent Token Refresh:</strong> Next.js edge middleware (<span class="highlight">src/proxy.ts</span>) intercepts requests to protected routes. If an access token has expired but a valid refresh token exists, it calls the internal <span class="highlight">/api/auth/refresh</span> endpoint in the background, updating cookies seamlessly without interrupting the user.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4.3 Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)</h2>
<p>
  Three privilege tiers are enforced at the edge middleware, server action, and database levels:
</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Role</th>
      <th>Permissions &amp; Scope</th>
      <th>Restricted Boundaries</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>super_admin</strong></td>
      <td>Full platform authority: user role promotion, system re-initialization, database management, and complete audit log inspection.</td>
      <td>Unrestricted.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>admin</strong></td>
      <td>Operational authority: CRUD management of services, blog articles, team members, testimonials, contact message inbox, and expense review.</td>
      <td>Cannot delete other administrators or access internal encryption keys.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>user</strong></td>
      <td>Client self-service: access to the Client Portal, profile management, service requests, and filing personal expense records.</td>
      <td>Blocked from <span class="highlight">/admin</span> routes; redirected automatically to <span class="highlight">/profile</span>.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- ══════════════════ SECTION 5 ══════════════════ -->
<h1>5. Hosting, Infrastructure &amp; Cloud Topology</h1>

<div class="card-box">
  <div class="card-box-title">Cloud Infrastructure Matrix</div>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Infrastructure Component</th>
        <th>Provider</th>
        <th>Configuration &amp; Specifications</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Application Server</strong></td>
        <td>Railway (PaaS)</td>
        <td>Nixpacks deployment engine. Configured with <span class="highlight">output: "standalone"</span> in <span class="highlight">next.config.ts</span> for minimal Docker image size and rapid container restarts.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Primary Database</strong></td>
        <td>Supabase (AWS Singapore)</td>
        <td>PostgreSQL 15+ cluster operating behind an AWS-hosted PgBouncer pooler. Supports SSL encryption and continuous point-in-time recovery.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Edge Object Storage</strong></td>
        <td>Cloudflare R2</td>
        <td>Zero egress fee S3-compatible storage bucket (<span class="highlight">accbot-main-website</span>) distributed across Cloudflare's global edge network.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Transactional Mail</strong></td>
        <td>Resend</td>
        <td>High-reputation email delivery infrastructure configured with custom domain verification (DKIM, SPF, DMARC).</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Source Control &amp; CI/CD</strong></td>
        <td>GitHub</td>
        <td>Automated continuous delivery pipeline triggering production builds on each push to the <span class="highlight">main</span> branch.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

