<!-- ══════════════════ SECTION 8 ══════════════════ -->
<h1>8. Operational Runbook &amp; Environment Reference</h1>

<h2>8.1 Required Environment Variables</h2>
<p>
  The following variables must be configured in Railway Project Variables:
</p>

<div class="code-block">DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.[ref]:[pwd]@aws-0-ap-southeast-1.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
JWT_SECRET=[64-character-random-hex-string]
JWT_ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRY=15m
JWT_REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRY=7d
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://accbots.up.railway.app
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=noreply@yourdomain.com
ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@yourdomain.com
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=[cloudflare-account-id]
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=[r2-access-key-id]
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=[r2-secret-access-key]
R2_BUCKET_NAME=accbot-main-website
R2_PUBLIC_URL=https://pub-xxxxxxxx.r2.dev
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=</div>

<h2>8.2 SQL Migration Execution Order</h2>
<p>
  When initializing or upgrading the PostgreSQL instance, execute the migration files in this precise sequence via the Supabase SQL Editor:
</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>supabase/schema.sql:</strong> Base tables, initial constraints, and triggers.</li>
  <li><strong>supabase/schema_v2.sql:</strong> Custom authentication migration (decoupling from Supabase Auth) and user management.</li>
  <li><strong>supabase/schema_v3.sql:</strong> Financial ledger, Chart of Accounts, journal entry splits, trial balance view, and expense tracker tables.</li>
  <li><strong>supabase/seed.sql:</strong> Initial website settings, default service packages, and demo advisory content.</li>
</ol>

